INSERT INTO `session_notes` VALUES (1,'2026-05-23 15:28:56.269236','General','High','### Historical Summary:\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s phonics and short vowel sounds session, Liam demonstrated high engagement and enthusiasm. He successfully navigated the short-story passage with ease, showcasing his ability to read fluently. Although he encountered some challenges with words containing the short \'o\' sound, such as \'flock\' and \'spot\', he demonstrated resilience and self-correction skills by accurately identifying and correcting the words on his second pass. This session reinforces Liam\'s progress in phonics and short vowel sounds, setting him up for continued success in his elementary education.','Elementary','Super enthusiastic today. Read through the short-story passage smoothly. Struggled slightly with words containing the short \'o\' sound like \'flock\' and \'spot\' but self-corrected quickly on the second pass.','Liam','Phonics and Short Vowel Sounds',NULL,NULL,NULL),(2,'2026-05-23 15:34:28.517580','Maryland','High','### Historical Summary:\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s session on Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis, Angad demonstrated high engagement and a strong understanding of the material. He approached the topic with a keen mind, showcasing his ability to differentiate between the two complex biological processes. Although he required some clarification on certain points, Angad\'s overall performance was commendable, reflecting his progress in understanding the intricacies of cellular biology.\r\n\r\nThis session aligns with the Maryland State Department of Education\'s standards for elementary science education, specifically addressing the following benchmarks:\r\n\r\n- 5.2.1: Students will be able to describe the basic needs of plants and animals, including the role of sunlight, water, and air.\r\n- 5.2.2: Students will be able to explain the process of photosynthesis and its importance in the ecosystem.\r\n- 5.2.3: Students will be able to describe the process of cellular respiration and its role in energy production.\r\n\r\nAngad\'s performance in this session reinforces his understanding of cellular biology, setting him up for continued success in his elementary education. To further reinforce his learning, we recommend that he review the flashcards created today for 10 minutes before our next session, ensuring a solid grasp of the key concepts and terminology.','Elementary','overall good','Angad','Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis',NULL,NULL,NULL),(3,'2026-05-23 15:59:31.898707','Maryland','High','### Session Summary:\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s mathematics session, Sarah Mitchell demonstrated high engagement and a strong work ethic, showcasing her ability to grasp complex concepts in the realm of fractions. Her mastery of multiplying fractions was particularly impressive, with 8 out of 10 problems solved correctly. However, she did encounter some challenges with mixed numbers, which she diligently worked to overcome by the end of the session.\r\n\r\nThis session aligns with the Maryland State Department of Education\'s standards for middle school mathematics education, specifically addressing the following benchmarks:\r\n\r\n- 6.1.1: Students will be able to apply mathematical concepts and procedures to solve problems involving fractions, decimals, and percents.\r\n- 6.1.2: Students will be able to demonstrate an understanding of the relationships between fractions, decimals, and percents.\r\n- 6.2.1: Students will be able to apply mathematical concepts and procedures to solve problems involving mixed numbers and complex fractions.\r\n\r\nSarah\'s performance in this session reinforces her understanding of fraction operations, setting her up for continued success in her middle school mathematics education. To further reinforce her learning, we recommend that she review the mixed number problems on worksheet page 15 for 15 minutes before our next session, ensuring a solid grasp of the key concepts and terminology.','Middle School','Mastered multiplication of fractions, solved 8 out of 10 problems correctly, struggled with mixed numbers but improved by end of session','Sarah Mitchell','Mathematics','2026-05-23','Tutor',NULL),(4,'2026-05-23 16:00:36.192826','Florida','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s reading session, Marcus Thompson demonstrated high engagement and a strong work ethic, showcasing his ability to navigate complex texts with enthusiasm. His independent reading of two passages was a notable achievement, as he effectively demonstrated comprehension of the first passage. However, he encountered some challenges with the second passage, losing focus midway through and requiring prompting to identify the main idea.\r\n\r\nThis session aligns with the Florida Department of Education\'s standards for elementary reading education, specifically addressing the following benchmarks:\r\n\r\n- ELA.L.6.1: Students will be able to cite textual evidence to support analysis, reflection, and research.\r\n- ELA.L.6.2: Students will be able to determine a theme or central idea of a text and analyze its development.\r\n- ELA.L.6.3: Students will be able to analyze in detail how a key sentence, paragraph, or section of text contributes to the development of the text\'s theme or central idea.\r\n\r\nMarcus\'s performance in this session reinforces his understanding of reading comprehension strategies, setting him up for continued success in his elementary reading education. To further reinforce his learning, we recommend that he re-read the second passage and write three sentences about the main idea, ensuring a solid grasp of the key concepts and terminology. This exercise will help him develop his ability to identify and articulate the central idea of a text, a crucial skill for future academic success.','Elementary','Read two passages independently, good comprehension on first passage, lost focus midway through second passage, needed prompting to identify main idea','Marcus Thompson','Reading','2026-05-23','Tutor 1',NULL),(5,'2026-05-23 16:02:43.820872','Maryland','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s algebra session, Priya Sharma demonstrated exceptional engagement and a keen understanding of the subject matter, showcasing her ability to tackle complex mathematical concepts confidently. Her independent work on linear equations was a notable achievement, as she effectively solved systems of equations with ease. Moreover, her thought-provoking questions about real-world applications of algebraic concepts highlighted her ability to think critically and make connections between theoretical knowledge and practical applications.\r\n\r\nThis session aligns with the Maryland Department of Education\'s standards for high school mathematics education, specifically addressing the following benchmarks:\r\n\r\n- HSA.SSE.A.1: Students will be able to explain the process of solving a linear equation and inequalities, and solve linear equations and inequalities, including those with variables on both sides.\r\n- HSA.SSE.B.4: Students will be able to solve systems of linear equations using substitution and elimination methods.\r\n- HSA.SSE.B.5: Students will be able to solve quadratic equations by factoring, completing the square, and using the quadratic formula.\r\n\r\nPriya\'s performance in this session reinforces her understanding of algebraic concepts, setting her up for continued success in her high school mathematics education. To further reinforce her learning, we recommend that she complete the practice set on quadratic equations in chapter 4, ensuring a solid grasp of the key concepts and terminology. This exercise will help her develop her ability to solve quadratic equations, a crucial skill for future academic success and real-world applications in science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM) fields.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n\r\n- Complete practice set on quadratic equations chapter 4\r\n- Review and apply concepts learned to real-world applications and problems\r\n- Be prepared to move on to more advanced algebraic concepts, including functions and graphing.','High School','Excellent understanding of linear equations, independently solved systems of equations, asked great questions about real world applications, ready to move to quadratic equations','Priya Sharma','Algebra','2026-05-23','Tutor 2',NULL),(6,'2026-05-23 16:04:29.613717','Maryland','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s elementary science session, Jake Williams demonstrated a high level of engagement, despite occasional distractions throughout the session. This enthusiasm is a testament to his innate curiosity and desire to learn. The session focused on the fundamental concepts of the water cycle, with Jake showing a willingness to absorb and process new information.\r\n\r\nWhile Jake demonstrated a basic understanding of the water cycle, there were notable areas for revision. Specifically, he struggled to recall the steps involved in evaporation and condensation, requiring further review and reinforcement. However, his response to visual diagrams was encouraging, suggesting that a more visual approach may be beneficial in his learning process.\r\n\r\nThis session aligns with the Maryland Department of Education\'s standards for elementary science education, specifically addressing the following benchmarks:\r\n\r\n- MS-ESS2-2: Students will be able to understand the water cycle, including the processes of evaporation, condensation, and precipitation.\r\n- MS-ESS2-3: Students will be able to explain the role of water in the Earth\'s systems, including the water cycle and the movement of water between the atmosphere, land, and oceans.\r\n\r\nTo further reinforce Jake\'s learning, we recommend that he complete the assigned homework task: watching a water cycle video and drawing a labeled diagram. This exercise will help him solidify his understanding of the water cycle and develop a deeper appreciation for the essential processes involved. By revisiting and reinforcing these concepts, Jake will be better equipped to tackle more complex scientific ideas in the future.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n\r\n- Complete homework task: watch water cycle video and draw a labeled diagram\r\n- Review and revise understanding of evaporation and condensation steps\r\n- Continue to explore and learn about the water cycle through interactive and visual approaches, such as diagrams and videos.','Elementary','Distracted throughout session, covered water cycle basics, could not recall evaporation and condensation steps, needs revision, responded better to visual diagrams than text','Jake Williams','Science','2026-05-23','Tutor 3',NULL),(7,'2026-05-23 16:05:53.949919','General','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s high school English session, Aisha Johnson demonstrated a high level of engagement, showcasing her enthusiasm for the subject matter and her dedication to improving her writing skills. The session focused on refining her essay structure, with Aisha producing a strong thesis statement that effectively set the tone for her argument.\r\n\r\nWhile Aisha\'s thesis statement was a notable strength, there were areas for revision in the development of her body paragraphs. Specifically, she struggled to incorporate supporting evidence to bolster her claims, highlighting the need for further attention to this aspect of her writing. Additionally, her conclusion required improvement, as it failed to effectively summarize her main points and provide a satisfying conclusion to her argument.\r\n\r\nNotwithstanding these areas for revision, Aisha demonstrated a commendable command of vocabulary throughout the session, using a range of words to convey her ideas and arguments. This proficiency in language use is a testament to her growing writing skills and her ability to express herself effectively.\r\n\r\nThis session aligns with the Maryland Department of Education\'s standards for high school English education, specifically addressing the following benchmarks:\r\n\r\n- HS-ELA-W.9-10.1: Students will be able to write arguments to support claims in an analysis of substantive topics or texts, using valid reasoning and relevant and sufficient evidence.\r\n- HS-ELA-W.9-10.5: Students will be able to use technology, including the internet, to produce and publish writing and to interact and collaborate with others.\r\n\r\nTo further reinforce Aisha\'s learning, we recommend that she complete the assigned homework task: revising her body paragraphs to include two evidence points each and bringing a revised draft to the next session. This exercise will help her solidify her understanding of effective essay structure and develop a deeper appreciation for the importance of supporting evidence in her writing.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n\r\n- Revise body paragraphs to include two evidence points each\r\n- Bring revised draft to the next session\r\n- Continue to develop and refine her writing skills, with a focus on incorporating supporting evidence and crafting effective conclusions.','High School','Worked on essay structure, strong thesis statement written, body paragraphs lack supporting evidence, conclusion needs improvement, good vocabulary usage throughout','Aisha Johnson','English','2026-05-23','Tutor 4',NULL),(8,'2026-05-23 17:12:13.512360','Maryland','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s reading session, Marcus Thompson demonstrated high engagement and overall good comprehension. He successfully read two passages independently, however, lost focus midway through the second passage and required prompting to identify the main idea. With guidance, Marcus was able to regain focus and complete the passage.\r\n\r\n### Maryland Curriculum Standard Reference: ELA.L.5.1 - Students will analyze in detail how a text\'s structure is used to develop its meaning.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps:\r\n- Review the flashcards created today for 10 minutes before our next session.\r\n- Practice identifying main ideas in short passages to improve comprehension.','Elementary','overall good','Marcus Thompson','Reading','2026-05-23','Tutor 4',NULL),(9,'2026-05-23 18:14:05.584827','Florida','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s high school English session, Angad demonstrated a good understanding of essay structure and vocabulary usage. However, he struggled to provide sufficient supporting evidence in his body paragraphs and needs to improve his conclusion. Angad\'s strong thesis statement was a notable highlight of his work.\r\n\r\n### Florida Standards for English Language Arts (LAFS) 9-10.1:\r\n\r\n* Write arguments to support claims in an analysis of substantive topics or texts, using valid reasoning and relevant and sufficient evidence.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Complete the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5.\r\n- Review and revise the essay to incorporate more supporting evidence and a stronger conclusion.','High School','overall good but can do more better','Angad','English','2026-05-23','Tutor 4',NULL),(10,'2026-05-23 19:11:25.770168','General','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nPriya Sharma showed high engagement during today\'s elementary English session. She demonstrated understanding of the main idea in the second passage but needs to work on providing supporting evidence. To improve her comprehension, Priya will focus on analyzing the text more critically.\r\n\r\n### Florida Standards for English Language Arts (ELA) K-5: RL.2.1, W.2.3\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Re-read the second passage and write 3 sentences about the main idea\r\n- Practice identifying supporting evidence in texts to enhance comprehension','Elementary','have not performed well. need extra efforts. but can do.','Priya Sharma','English','2026-05-23','Tutor 3',NULL),(11,'2026-05-23 19:12:29.647757','General','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nPriya Sharma showed high engagement during today\'s elementary English session. She demonstrated understanding of the main idea in the second passage but needs to work on providing supporting evidence. To improve her comprehension, Priya will focus on analyzing the text more critically.\r\n\r\n### Florida Standards for English Language Arts (ELA) K-5: RL.2.1, W.2.3\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Re-read the second passage and write 3 sentences about the main idea\r\n- Practice identifying supporting evidence in texts to enhance comprehension','Elementary','have not performed well. need extra efforts. but can do.','Priya Sharma','English','2026-05-23','Tutor 3',NULL),(12,'2026-05-23 19:20:01.401478','Florida','Medium','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s mathematics session, Emily demonstrated a good understanding of the subject matter, showcasing her knowledge in a medium-engagement environment. She was able to work through various problems with ease, although some areas still require practice. Overall, the session was productive, and Emily showed promise in her math skills.\r\n\r\n### Florida Standards for Mathematics (FSA-M) 6.RP.3: Reasoning about equivalent ratios.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n* Practice mixed number problems on worksheet page 15\r\n* Review and apply the concept of equivalent ratios in real-world scenarios.','Middle School','nice student, good knowledge of the subject. did great in todays session!!','Emily','Mathematics','2026-05-23','Tutor 1',NULL),(13,'2026-05-23 19:20:50.903004','Maryland','High','### Historical Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s session on Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis, Marcus Thompson demonstrated high engagement and a strong understanding of the material. He effectively compared and contrasted the two processes, showcasing his ability to think critically. Marcus also created flashcards to aid in his learning, a great strategy for retention. His enthusiasm and participation made the session enjoyable and productive.\r\n\r\nMaryland\'s Life Science curriculum standard (MS-LS1-1) emphasizes the ability to explain the role of cells in living organisms, which was a key focus of today\'s discussion.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Review the flashcards created today for 10 minutes before our next session.\r\n- Complete the accompanying worksheet on Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis to reinforce understanding.','Elementary','nice student. good job','Marcus Thompson','Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis','2026-05-23','Tutor 1',NULL),(14,'2026-05-24 08:24:18.623602','Florida','Medium','### Historical Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s session on Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis, Liam demonstrated a medium level of engagement, actively participating in discussions and asking relevant questions. He showed a good understanding of the material, particularly in identifying key differences between the two processes. Liam\'s notes and diagrams also reflected his attention to detail and organization skills.\r\n\r\n**Florida Standards for Middle School Science (NGSSS): 5.L.1.1-5.L.1.3**\r\n\r\n* Complete the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5.\r\n* Review and summarize key points from the session to prepare for the next class.','Middle School','nice session','Liam','Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis','2026-05-24','Angad',NULL),(15,'2026-05-24 16:29:21.784711','Florida','Medium','### Historical Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s session on Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis, Angad demonstrated a medium level of engagement, actively participating in discussions and showing a nice understanding of the concepts. He demonstrated a bright student\'s ability to grasp complex ideas. With some revision, Angad will solidify his understanding of these processes.\r\n\r\n### Curriculum Standard Reference (Florida Standards for Science, 5th Grade: SC.5.L.13.1)\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Angad will revise the topics taught today to solidify his understanding.\r\n- He will complete additional practice problems to reinforce his knowledge of Cellular Respiration and Photosynthesis.','Middle School','Nice understanding power and a bright student ','Angad','CSE','2026-05-24','Suraj Singh',NULL),(16,'2026-05-24 16:30:44.227450','Maryland','Low','## Session Summary\r\n\r\nToday\'s mathematics session with Liam focused on reinforcing multiplication concepts. Despite initial difficulties, Liam showed improvement by the end of the session, demonstrating a better understanding of the material. However, his behavior during the session was concerning, and we will need to address this issue in future sessions.\r\n\r\n## Curriculum Standard Reference: Maryland State Department of Education, Mathematics Curriculum Standards (Grade 3) - 3.OA.7\r\n\r\n## Next Steps\r\n- Complete the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5.\r\n- Work on maintaining a respectful attitude during sessions.','Elementary','Need to work on his behaviour. Got very rude between the session.','Liam','Mathematics','2026-05-24','Suraj Singh',NULL),(17,'2026-05-24 19:12:43.853924','Maryland','Low','### Historical Summary\r\n\r\nToday\'s session with Liam focused on Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis, where he showed a nice session despite low engagement. Liam demonstrated a good understanding of the material, but required additional support to stay engaged. I created flashcards with him to aid in his comprehension. With practice, Liam will solidify his grasp of these essential biological processes.\r\n\r\n### Maryland Curriculum Standard Reference: MS-LS1-8 (HS-LS2-6)\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n• Review the flashcards created today for 10 minutes before our next session.\r\n• Practice summarizing the key differences between Cellular Respiration and Photosynthesis.','Elementary','nice session','Liam','Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis','2026-05-24','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(18,'2026-05-24 19:15:50.488686','Maryland','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s mathematics session, Marcus Thompson demonstrated a high level of engagement and enthusiasm. He showed a strong understanding of multiplication concepts, accurately solving 7 out of 10 problems. His confidence in calculations improved significantly, particularly with multi-digit numbers. By the end of the session, Marcus had made notable progress in mastering this key skill.\r\n\r\n### Curriculum Standard Reference: Maryland State Department of Education, Mathematics Curriculum Standards for Elementary School (Grade 3-5)\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Complete the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5.\r\n- Review mixed number calculations to solidify understanding.','Elementary','nice nice nice','Marcus Thompson','Mathematics','2026-05-24','Suraj Singh',NULL),(19,'2026-05-24 19:20:25.278147','Maryland','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nToday\'s elementary English session with Liam focused on developing his writing skills. He demonstrated a high level of engagement and understanding of the topics covered in class. However, he needs to work on incorporating supporting evidence in his body paragraphs and improving his conclusion. Liam showed great potential in using good vocabulary throughout his writing.\r\n\r\n### Maryland Curriculum Standard Reference: \r\nELA.K-5.W.3: Write narratives to develop real or imagined experiences or events using effective technique, descriptive details, and clear structure.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Liam will revise the topics taught today for better understanding.\r\n- He will practice incorporating supporting evidence in his writing.','Elementary','nice lecture on English','Liam','English','2026-05-25','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(20,'2026-05-24 19:20:55.326309','Maryland','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s mathematics session, Marcus Thompson demonstrated a high level of engagement, actively participating in discussions and showing enthusiasm for learning. He successfully completed the multiplication of single-digit numbers by multi-digit numbers, applying his understanding of place value. Marcus\'s confidence in solving math problems grew throughout the session.\r\n\r\n### Maryland Curriculum Standard Reference: \r\nMaryland\'s Mathematics curriculum emphasizes the development of problem-solving skills and mathematical reasoning (MSDE, 2020).\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Complete the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5.\r\n- Review and practice multiplication of multi-digit numbers by single-digit numbers.','Elementary','nice lecture with Marcus','Marcus Thompson','Mathematics','2026-05-24','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(21,'2026-05-24 19:21:20.425795','Maryland','High','### Historical Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s session on Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis, Marcus Thompson demonstrated high engagement and a strong understanding of the material. He effectively distinguished between the two processes, showing a clear grasp of their similarities and differences. Marcus\'s enthusiasm and participation were notable throughout the session. His revision of the topics taught today will further solidify his understanding.\r\n\r\n**Maryland Curriculum Standard: 5.1B - Explain the processes of photosynthesis and cellular respiration.**\r\n\r\n### Next Steps:\r\n• Review notes on cellular respiration and photosynthesis\r\n• Complete a diagram illustrating the two processes','Elementary','nice','Marcus Thompson','Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis','2026-05-24','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(22,'2026-05-24 19:24:13.113955','General','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s reading session, Priya Sharma demonstrated a high level of engagement as she navigated through the assigned passages. She showed good comprehension of the first passage but lost focus midway through the second passage, requiring prompting to identify the main idea. With guidance, Priya was able to refocus and complete the task.\r\n\r\n### Curriculum Standard Reference\r\nThis session aligns with the Florida Standards for English Language Arts (8.RL.1, 8.RL.2), which emphasize close reading and comprehension skills.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Re-read the second passage to improve retention and comprehension.\r\n- Write 3 sentences about the main idea of the second passage.','Middle School','nice session on reading','Priya Sharma','Reading','2026-05-24','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(23,'2026-05-24 19:25:02.989996','Florida','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nPriya Sharma demonstrated high engagement during today\'s high school science session. The lesson focused on mixed number problems, and Priya showed a good understanding of the concepts, especially when visual diagrams were used to support the learning. With practice, Priya should be able to apply these skills to more complex problems.\r\n\r\n### Curriculum Standard Reference: \r\nFlorida\'s B.E.S.T. Standards for Mathematics (2020) emphasizes the importance of understanding and applying rational numbers, including mixed numbers, in various mathematical operations.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps:\r\n- Practice mixed number problems on worksheet page 15\r\n- Review and apply concepts to word problems in the next session','High School','nice ','Priya Sharma','Science','2026-05-24','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(24,'2026-05-24 19:25:55.916743','Maryland','High','### Historical Summary\r\n\r\nToday\'s session on Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis with Liam was engaging and productive. He demonstrated a good understanding of the material, showing promise in distinguishing between these two essential biological processes. Liam\'s participation and questions were valuable in shaping the discussion. Overall, it was a nice session.\r\n\r\n### Curriculum Standard Reference: \r\nMaryland\'s Next Generation Science Standards (NGSS) emphasize understanding the interconnectedness of life processes, including cellular respiration and photosynthesis.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Review the flashcards created today for 10 minutes before our next session.\r\n- Complete a short quiz on cellular respiration and photosynthesis concepts at home.','Elementary','nice session','Liam','Cellular Respiration vs Photosynthesis','2026-05-25','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(25,'2026-05-24 19:36:55.646678','Maryland','Low','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nToday\'s science session with Marcus Thompson focused on reinforcing water cycle basics. Although engagement was low, visual diagrams proved effective in capturing his attention. However, it\'s clear that he still requires revision on the evaporation and condensation steps. A more interactive approach may be necessary to boost engagement in future sessions.\r\n\r\n### Maryland Curriculum Standard Reference: \r\nMaryland College and Career Ready Standards for Science (MS-ESS2-1)\r\n\r\n### Next Steps:\r\n* Review water cycle diagram with Marcus to reinforce understanding of evaporation and condensation steps\r\n* Prepare interactive activities for future sessions to increase engagement','Elementary','awesome session','Marcus Thompson','Science','2026-05-25','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(26,'2026-05-24 19:39:58.039897','Maryland','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s elementary English session, Emily demonstrated high engagement and enthusiasm for learning. She showed a good understanding of language concepts, but needed guidance on applying them effectively. Emily\'s vocabulary usage was strong, but her writing lacked supporting evidence and a clear conclusion. \r\n\r\n### Maryland Curriculum Standard Reference: (ELA.K.1-2.1, ELA.K.2-3.1) - Reading and writing skills are foundational to language arts.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps:\r\n- Complete the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5.\r\n- Review and revise Emily\'s writing to include supporting evidence and a clear conclusion.','Elementary','nice english session','Emily','English','2026-05-25','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(27,'2026-05-24 19:44:09.861951','Maryland','High','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s elementary English session with Marcus Thompson, we focused on building a strong narrative structure. Marcus showed enthusiasm and creativity in his writing, but needs to work on adding supporting details to his story. He demonstrated a good understanding of vocabulary usage and showed promise in developing his writing skills.\r\n\r\n### Maryland Curriculum Standard Reference: ELA.L.6.1 - Use evidence from texts to support analysis, reflection, and research.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n- Complete the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5.\r\n- Review and revise Marcus\'s story to incorporate more descriptive details.','Elementary','beautiful session','Marcus Thompson','English','2026-05-25','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(33,'2026-05-24 20:13:24.593739','Maryland','Low','### Session Summary\r\n\r\nDuring today\'s elementary English session, Liam struggled to engage with the material. To improve his writing skills, we focused on developing a clear thesis statement and organizing essay structure. Although Liam showed potential, his body paragraphs lacked supporting evidence and the conclusion needed refinement. He demonstrated good vocabulary usage throughout the session.\r\n\r\n### Maryland Curriculum Standard Reference: \r\nEnglish Language Arts (ELA) Standards for Elementary School (Maryland College and Career-Ready Standards for English Language Arts, 2010)\r\n\r\n### Next Steps:\r\n- Review the flashcards created today for 10 minutes before our next session.\r\n- Bring a sample essay to the next session for peer review and feedback.','Elementary','nice','Liam','English','2026-05-25','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(34,'2026-05-24 20:34:16.590654','Florida','Medium','During today\'s middle school English session, Liam demonstrated a good understanding of the topics covered. However, his engagement was only medium, indicating a need for increased participation. To improve, Liam should focus on developing his critical thinking skills and providing supporting evidence in his writing. This will enable him to strengthen his arguments and produce high-quality work.\r\n\r\nFlorida Standards for English Language Arts (LAFS) 6-8.1\r\n\r\nNext Steps\r\n* Liam will revise the topics taught today for better understanding.\r\n* He will practice writing with supporting evidence to enhance his arguments.','Middle School','Session held great and student can do better.','Liam','English','2026-05-25','Angad Dhiman',NULL),(35,'2026-06-02 14:14:23.620679','Florida','Medium','During today\'s high school medicinal sciences session, student 1 demonstrated a strong foundation in the subject matter, showcasing a fabulous overall performance. Their attentiveness and engagement were notable, indicating a good grasp of the concepts covered. However, there is room for improvement, as evidenced by the medium engagement level. To further solidify their understanding, it is essential for student 1 to thoroughly revise the topics taught today.\r\n\r\n**Florida\'s Next Generation Sunshine State Standards for Science (NGSSS)**\r\n\r\n* Revise all the topic taught today\r\n* Complete assigned readings on pharmacology and anatomy for the next session','High School','1. Student was attentive.\r\n2. Overall performance is fabulous.','student 1','Medicinal sciences','2026-06-02','User 1',NULL),(36,'2026-06-11 16:40:46.008089','Florida','High','Brandon was very distracted today, leaving and rejoining the session about 5 times, getting up out of his seat, and drawing on the board after I asked him to stop. I have definitely seen better days with him. I hope he gets better. In terms of the material, he did a great job with rounding and the area model once he was focused - he even showed a solid understanding of the area model with a 3-digit by 1-digit problem. However, he still needs to work on his 6s, 7s, 8s, 9s multiplication facts because he was not sure what 8x6 was. Reviewing multiplication flashcards at home for 6s-9s is definitely a priority for next time, and I plan to continue working with him on area model problems.','3','Very distracted today, left/rejoined online session 5 times\r\n\r\nConstantly getting up out of his seat and drawing on the interactive board after being asked to stop\r\n\r\nSolid progress with rounding rules and utilizing the area model once focused\r\n\r\nStruggles heavily with multiplication facts for 6, 7, 8, and 9 (e.g., could not recall 8x6)','Brandon','Student','2026-06-11','Suraj Singh',NULL),(37,'2026-06-11 18:53:14.467876','Common Core','High','I had a great session with Marcus today. He was very focused and engaged, which was a welcome change from some of our previous sessions. He did a great job with the area model, especially when we moved to 3-digit by 1-digit multiplication - he was able to visualize the problem and find the product quickly. However, he still struggles with his 9s multiplication facts, and it showed when he got 9x9 wrong, telling me he was unsure of the product. I also noticed that he tends to rely on counting up when multiplying multi-digit numbers, which is a habit we\'ll need to work on breaking. Overall, it was a productive session, and I\'m looking forward to continuing to work with him on building his fluency with multiplication facts and developing more efficient strategies for multi-digit multiplication.','','nice session','Marcus Thompson','Student','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(38,'2026-06-11 19:02:41.987898','Common Core','High','Today we started the session by reviewing loops and conditional statements using the Blooket platform, which the students were engaged with and seemed to understand the concepts. We then moved on to practicing mixed number problems, where Aarav helped Priya debug her syntax errors, and Kabir completed the array traversal challenge first, showing a good grasp of the material. The students worked well together, with a highly collaborative dynamic. After reviewing mixed numbers, we finished the session with an array traversal challenge on IXL, where the students were able to apply what they learned about loops and conditional statements. I plan to continue working with the students on mixed number problems next session, specifically focusing on practice with worksheet page 15.','7','Introduced loops and conditional statements. Aarav helped debug Priya\'s syntax errors. Kabir completed the array traversal challenge first. Group dynamics were highly collaborative.','Aarav Mehta, Priya Patel, Kabir Singh','Overall','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(39,'2026-06-11 19:22:31.571237','Common Core','High','I\'m really impressed with Kabir today - he demonstrated fantastic understanding of the area model, even with 3-digit by 2-digit multiplication. He answered the exit ticket wrong because he told me he had a hard time lining up all of the numbers properly. His final product was wrong, but he caught his mistake. I\'m glad to see him being more methodical in his approach, but it\'s evident he still needs to work on his fact fluency because he was not sure what 7x6 was, even though he\'s been practicing. I plan to give him more mixed number problems to work on, especially those on worksheet page 15, to help him solidify his understanding and build his confidence.','','Introduced loops and conditional statements. Aarav helped debug Priya\'s syntax errors. Kabir completed the array traversal challenge first. Group dynamics were highly collaborative.','arav Mehta, Priya Patel, Kabir Singh','Student','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(40,'2026-06-11 19:26:24.089719','Florida','High','Today we covered loops and conditional statements, and the students really engaged with the material. We started with an ice breaker question that got everyone thinking about their favorite video games, then moved on to a collaborative coding challenge where Aarav helped Priya debug her syntax errors, and Kabir completed the array traversal challenge first, which was impressive. The group dynamics were highly collaborative, and everyone was working together to help each other out. We then worked through a practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5, and the students did well with the loops, but needed some extra help with the conditional statements. To reinforce their understanding, I asked them to complete a Blooket on the topic, which they did with some effort, and I noticed that Priya still needed a bit of extra help, so I made a note to work with her individually next session.','2','Introduced loops and conditional statements. Aarav helped debug Priya\'s syntax errors. Kabir completed the array traversal challenge first. Group dynamics were highly collaborative.','Aarav Mehta, Priya Patel, Kabir Singh','Overall','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(41,'2026-06-11 19:29:49.349527','Florida','High','Today we started the session with an ice breaker question, which the students enthusiastically participated in. We then moved on to working with loops and conditional statements, where the students were introduced to a new concept. The students were highly engaged and worked well together, with Aarav helping Priya debug her syntax errors and Kabir completing the array traversal challenge first. We played a game of Penguin Run to break up the lesson and keep the students energized. After that, we worked on a math tic-tac-toe challenge, where the students showed a good understanding of the concept. We finished the session with a Blooket review, where the students showed a good grasp of the material. The students\' high level of engagement and collaboration was evident throughout the session, and I look forward to continuing to work with them on this topic next session.','','Introduced loops and conditional statements. Aarav helped debug Priya\'s syntax errors. Kabir completed the array traversal challenge first. Group dynamics were highly collaborative.','Aarav Mehta, Priya Patel, Kabir Singh','Overall','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(42,'2026-06-12 06:39:22.171642','Florida','High','Today we covered loops and conditional statements, and the students did well with the introduction. We started with a collaborative ice breaker, then moved on to a Penguin Run game where Aarav helped debug Priya\'s syntax errors, and Kabir completed the array traversal challenge first. After, we worked through a practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5, where the students showed a good understanding of the concepts. I was impressed with their ability to work together and help each other out, which is a great sign of their collaborative dynamics. We finished the session by having them complete a Blooket on loops and conditional statements, and they all seemed to grasp the material well.','','Introduced loops and conditional statements. Aarav helped debug Priya\'s syntax errors. Kabir completed the array traversal challenge first. Group dynamics were highly collaborative.','Aarav Mehta, Priya Patel, Kabir Singh','Overall','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(43,'2026-06-12 06:40:01.305287','Florida','High','Liam had a great session today, he was fully engaged and on task the entire time. We worked on mixed number problems and he did a fantastic job with converting between improper fractions and mixed numbers. He struggled a bit with reducing fractions, particularly with the problem 12/8, but after some guidance, he was able to simplify it correctly. I also noticed he made a mistake on the worksheet when adding 3 1/2 + 2 3/4, he forgot to convert the mixed numbers to improper fractions before adding, but he caught his error and reworked the problem correctly. I will have him practice mixed number problems on worksheet page 15 next session to reinforce his understanding.','2','great session','Liam','Student','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(44,'2026-06-12 06:43:01.402740','Florida','Low','Today\'s session was a great one, and we made good progress on division concepts. We started with a \"Would You Rather\" ice breaker question, which got the students engaged and thinking critically. After that, we worked through some division word problems on IXL, and the students did well. Priya and Kabir both showed a good understanding of the concept, while Aarav needed a bit more time to grasp it. As per their request, we moved on to division with remainders, and I explained how to solve a division problem with remainders. The students needed some help with this, but they started to understand it more. I asked them to solve a division exit ticket for me, and unfortunately, they all got it incorrect because they were rushing. We will continue to go over division next session, focusing on foundational division facts and practicing with IXL and Blooket.','1','great session','Aarav Mehta, Priya Patel, Kabir Singh','Overall','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(45,'2026-06-12 06:48:55.495003','Florida','High','Liam had a great session today - he was fully engaged and on task the entire time. I was impressed with how quickly he picked up on the concept of finding the area of a rectangle with a length of 24 and a width of 6, using the area model. He even caught a mistake I made on the board and politely pointed it out. However, when it came to the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5, he struggled with the division problems, particularly with dividing by 6 and 9, as he got the product of the quotient and remainder wrong. I think he needs to work on his division facts, especially with those tricky numbers.','6','nice session with LIAM','Liam','Student','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(46,'2026-06-12 06:53:22.785677','Maryland','High','Angad had a very nice session today - he was fully engaged the entire time and was able to stay focused on the material. We worked on completing the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5, and he did a great job with simplifying trigonometric expressions, particularly with the Pythagorean identity. He still needs some practice with solving equations that involve inverse trig functions because he got stuck on question 3, which involved finding the value of x in the equation sin^(-1)(x) = pi/6. I\'m glad to see him making progress, and I\'m looking forward to continuing to work with him on this topic tomorrow.','Precalculus','very nice session','Angad','Student','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(47,'2026-06-12 07:13:08.292626','Common Core','High','Angad was very disappointing today - he seemed completely disengaged and uninterested in the material. I tried to get him to focus on completing the practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5, but he kept getting up and walking around the room, and at one point, he even pulled out his phone and started texting. I had to remind him multiple times to put it away. In terms of the math, he struggled with simplifying expressions with exponents, specifically when the bases were different. He got stuck on a problem that required him to multiply 3^2 by 2^3, and he didn\'t even attempt to simplify the expression. He also had trouble factoring quadratic expressions, and I had to show him how to do it multiple times. Despite my best efforts, he just didn\'t seem to be paying attention or putting in the effort to learn.','Algebra','very disappointing session','Angad','Student','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(48,'2026-06-12 07:14:52.426256','Florida','High','Today\'s session was a great start to our multiplication and division unit. We started with a \"Would You Rather\" ice breaker question which got the students engaged and laughing. After that, we worked through some multiplication word problems on IXL, and the students did well with them. Emily and Tom were quick to grasp the concepts, while Angad needed a bit more time to understand. We then moved on to division, and I introduced how to solve a division problem with remainders. Liam seemed to grasp it quickly, but the others needed some help understanding the concept. We finished the session with a division exit ticket, and unfortunately, they all got the same incorrect answer due to rushing. We will continue to work on division next session, focusing on helping them understand remainders and solve problems more accurately.','4','nice students and attentive','Liam, Emily, Tom, Angad','Overall','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(49,'2026-06-12 07:26:26.411964','Common Core','High','Angad was absolutely phenomenal today - he\'s definitely one of my favorite students ever. He picked up on the area model for 3-digit by 2-digit multiplication right away and did an amazing job with it, even when I threw in some multi-step problems. He still struggles with his 6s, 7s, 8s, and 9s multiplication facts, though - he got 6x7 wrong, saying it was 40 instead of 42 - but he was able to use the area model to help him solve the problem and get the right answer.','7','Best student ever!!!','Angad','Student','2026-06-12','Tutor_1',NULL),(50,'2026-06-12 07:42:45.477655','Common Core','Low','Today\'s session was challenging, and the students struggled to stay engaged. We started with a math tic-tac-toe warm-up game, but it ended in a tie, which didn\'t really get them excited about the session. After that, we moved on to working through a practice worksheet on page 14, questions 1 to 5, which they were supposed to complete. Unfortunately, they didn\'t seem to be paying attention, and as a result, they missed some key concepts. Aarav\'s laptop was also having some issues, which took up a bit of time. We then tried to move on to a Blooket, but Priya\'s headset kept disconnecting, and Kabir seemed to be having trouble with the questions. Despite these technical issues, we managed to get through a few questions, but it was clear that they weren\'t fully understanding the concepts. I will need to review the session and come up with a plan to better engage them in the next session.','','session was not good','Aarav Mehta, Priya Patel, Kabir Singh','Overall','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(51,'2026-06-12 13:43:26.629025','Common Core','High','Liam was super engaged today, and I loved seeing his enthusiasm when we played the ice-breaker task - he really lit up. However, when it came to evaluating expressions with parentheses, he struggled to get it right. He kept forgetting to follow the order of operations and was getting confused about which numbers to multiply first. I tried breaking it down step by step with him, but he still had trouble simplifying expressions like 3(2+5). On the other hand, he did a great job with multi-step evaluations, and it was clear he understood how to work through those problems. I\'m planning to focus on parentheses and order of operations tomorrow, and I\'ll also make sure to review some of the concepts he\'s been struggling with in a more concrete way.','','Liam do not evaluate expression correct using parenthesis.\r\nAlso able to evaluate multi step evaluation.\r\nLiam was excited to play ice-breaker task. Overall session held great.','Liam','Student','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(52,'2026-06-12 13:46:54.519751','Common Core','High','Today\'s session was a productive one, as we covered loops and conditional statements in our programming unit. The students started off strong, diving right into the array traversal challenge on IXL, with Kabir completing it first and Aarav and Priya close behind. After that, we moved on to the Blooket review, where they did well in identifying loops and conditionals. We then played a collaborative game of Penguin Run, where they had to work together to solve a series of problems. The students were highly engaged and worked well together, with Aarav and Priya helping each other out when they got stuck. We finished up the session by reviewing the topics we covered, and I\'m pleased to see that they seem to have a solid grasp on the concepts. Next session, we\'ll be revisiting the array traversal challenge and introducing more complex conditional statements.','5','Introduced loops and conditional statements. Aarav helped debug Priya\'s syntax errors. Kabir completed the array traversal challenge first. Group dynamics were highly collaborative.','Aarav Mehta, Priya Patel, Kabir Singh','Overall','2026-06-12','Suraj Singh',NULL),(53,'2026-06-16 18:55:14.859177','Florida','High','We focused on Florida 4 standards for Liam. Today\'s session was a blast, and I\'m thrilled to see Liam\'s high level of engagement! He was super excited to play the ice-breaker task, which got us both pumped up for the math work ahead. In terms of the material, Liam did a fantastic job with rounding whole numbers from 0 to 10,000 to the nearest 10, 100, or 1,000, as per Standard MA.4.NSO.1.4. However, I did notice that he struggled with evaluating expressions correctly using parentheses, which we\'ll need to work on in our next session. On the other hand, he showed great skill in evaluating multi-step expressions, which is a','4','[Standard MA.4.NSO.1.4: Round whole numbers from 0 to 10,000 to the nearest 10, 100 or 1,000.]\r\n\r\nAdditional Notes:\r\nLiam do not evaluate expression correct using parenthesis.\r\n Also able to evaluate multi step evaluation.\r\n Liam was excited to play ice-breaker task. Overall session held great.','Liam','Student','2026-06-17','Suraj Singh',NULL),(54,'2026-06-16 19:38:58.202644','Florida','Low','Liam had a tough time today, to be honest. He was pretty distracted and it was hard to keep him focused. I tried to make the session as engaging as possible, but it just wasn\'t his day. In terms of the material, we were working on comparing fractions, which is a tough topic for anyone, let alone a 4th grader. He struggled to plot and order fractions with different numerators and denominators, and it was clear he needed some extra help. I\'m glad we were able to get in some practice, even if it wasn\'t as productive as I had hoped. I\'m looking forward to seeing him again tomorrow and hopefully having a better session.','4','[Standard MA.4.FR.1.4: Plot, order and compare fractions, including mixed numbers and fractions greater than one, with different numerators and different denominators.]\r\n\r\nAdditional Notes:\r\nnice session','Liam','Student','2026-06-17','Suraj Singh',NULL),(55,'2026-06-16 19:49:34.363153','Florida','Medium','Liam had a pretty average session today, nothing too exciting but nothing too bad either. He\'s a Florida 3 student, and we focused on rounding whole numbers, which is a skill he can definitely improve on. He struggled a bit at first with rounding to the nearest 10 and 100, but with some extra practice problems, he started to get the hang of it by the end of the session. I think he just needs to work on his fluency with the numbers, because when he gets stuck, he tends to rely on counting up instead of using the actual rounding rules. I\'m looking forward to seeing him make some progress in this area, and I\'ll make sure to give him some more practice problems to work on at home','3','[Standard MA.3.NSO.1.4: Round whole numbers from 0 to 1,000 to the nearest 10 or 100.]\r\n\r\nAdditional Notes:\r\nnice session , student can do better','Liam','Student','2026-06-17','Suraj Singh',NULL),(56,'2026-06-16 19:59:40.310521','Common Core','High','I had an amazing session with Marcus Thompson today. He was super engaged and gave it his all, even when he got a bit misbehaved in between. I loved seeing his interest in decimals to thousandths - he really nailed it, especially when we practiced reading and writing decimals in base-ten numerals and expanded form. He was able to break down numbers like 347.392 into hundreds, tens, ones, tenths, hundredths, and thousandths, which was a huge accomplishment. With a bit more practice, I\'m confident he\'ll be a pro at this in no time.','','[Standard 5.NBT.A.3a: Read and write decimals to thousandths using base-ten numerals, number names, and expanded form, e.g., 347.392 = 3 x 100 + 4 x 10 + 7 x 1 + 3 x (1/10) + 9 x (1/100) + 2 x (1/1000).]\r\n\r\nAdditional Notes:\r\nwow whata session. Misbehaved in between but still coped up and gave his 100%. \r\nMarcus nailed it. I Loved Marcus interest.....!!','Marcus Thompson','Student','2026-06-17','Crack Tutor',NULL),(57,'2026-06-16 20:01:28.865789','Common Core','High','I had a fantastic session with Marcus Thompson today. He was super engaged and did a great job with constructing a linear function to model a relationship between two quantities, which is exactly what we focused on. He was able to determine the rate of change and initial value of the function from a description of a relationship, and even from two (x, y) values that we read from a table. I was impressed by how well he interpreted the rate of change and initial value in terms of the situation it models, and in terms of its graph or a table of values. Overall, it was a nice session and I\'m looking forward to seeing him continue to build on this concept.','8','[Standard 8.F.B.4: Construct a function to model a linear relationship between two quantities. Determine the rate of change and initial value of the function from a description of a relationship or from two (x, y) values, including reading these from a table or from a graph. Interpret the rate of change and initial value of a linear function in terms of the situation it models, and in terms of its graph or a table of values.]\r\n\r\nAdditional Notes:\r\nnice session','Marcus Thompson','Student','2026-06-17','Crack Tutor',NULL),(58,'2026-06-16 20:06:56.146551','Florida','High','Angad was fantastic today - I\'m so glad to have him in my sessions. He was super engaged and had a great attitude, which made our time together really enjoyable. We focused on rounding whole numbers, and he picked it up quickly, especially when we practiced rounding numbers to the nearest 10, 100, and 1,000. He did a great job with the area model too, even with larger numbers like 3-digit by 2-digit multiplication. I\'m looking forward to seeing his progress in this area and continuing to work with him on his math skills.','4','[Standard MA.4.NSO.1.4: Round whole numbers from 0 to 10,000 to the nearest 10, 100 or 1,000.]\r\n\r\nAdditional Notes:\r\nFantastic student. Excited